@startuml
title ExitPass Payment-to-Exit Fiscal Sequence

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam participantPadding 24
skinparam boxPadding 12

actor "Parker / operator" as User
participant "Payment channel\nWebPay / APM / Cashier /\nEC / operator-assisted" as Channel
participant "Payment Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
participant "Central PMS" as PMS
participant "Resolved Site\nPOS Server" as POS
participant "Gate / exit execution" as Gate
participant "Vendor PMS /\nHikCentral" as Vendor

User -> Channel : Initiate or complete\npayment flow
Channel -> Orchestrator : Submit payment outcome /\nprovider reference
Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : Verify provider outcome
Orchestrator -> PMS : Report verified outcome
PMS -> PMS : Record payment finality
PMS -> POS : Request Sales Invoice issuance\nfor resolved Site
POS -> POS : Issue Sales Invoice\nand fiscal records
POS --> PMS : Fiscal document\nidentity / status
PMS -> PMS : Record fiscal issuance reference
PMS -> Gate : Issue ExitAuthorization
Gate -> Gate : Consume ExitAuthorization
PMS -> Vendor : Synchronize payment / exit state
Vendor --> PMS : Acknowledgment / sync status

note over PMS,POS
No Sales Invoice, no ExitAuthorization,
unless a supervised, incident-tagged exception
is allowed by policy.
end note

note over Vendor
Vendor acknowledgment is synchronization.
It is not payment finality or exit authority.
end note

@enduml
